<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#FFFFFF', position: 'relative' }}>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 0, left: 0, width: 1280, height: 64, background: '#1E4FA8', flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', paddingLeft: 44, paddingRight: 44 }}>
    <Text style={{ color: '#FFFFFF', fontSize: 26, fontWeight: 'bold' }}>Four questions a radiochemist would actually ask</Text>
    <Text style={{ color: '#C9D9F2', fontSize: 14, marginLeft: 'auto' }}>02 · Research questions</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 88, left: 60, width: 1160, background: '#E8EFF8', padding: '13px 20px', boxSizing: 'border-box' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17.5, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.4 }}>Published FAP QSAR models report <span style={{ fontWeight: 'bold' }}>random-split R² ≈ 0.75</span>. That answers an interpolation question — the four questions below are what a design decision actually depends on.</Text>
  </Box>
  {[
    { x: 60, y: 208, n: 'RQ1', q: 'How accurate is a FAP affinity model under real use?', d: 'Random vs scaffold vs time split: interpolation, scaffold hopping, prospective prediction.' },
    { x: 664, y: 208, n: 'RQ2', q: 'Does paralogue bioactivity transfer to FAP?', d: 'PREP and DPP4 have 1.3x and 11x more data; can selectivity be predicted at all?' },
    { x: 60, y: 382, n: 'RQ3', q: 'When are the uncertainty estimates honest?', d: 'Applicability-domain gating plus split-conformal intervals at the 80% and 90% levels.' },
    { x: 664, y: 382, n: 'RQ4', q: 'What does multi-objective design add?', d: 'Graph GA with NSGA-II over affinity, margin, QED and SA, against two controls.' },
  ].map((c) => (
    <Box key={c.n} style={{ position: 'absolute', top: c.y, left: c.x, width: 556, height: 148, border: '1px solid #D6DCE5', padding: '16px 20px', boxSizing: 'border-box', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8' }}>{c.n}</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 18.5, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230', marginTop: 5, lineHeight: 1.3 }}>{c.q}</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, color: '#4A5568', marginTop: 7, lineHeight: 1.4 }}>{c.d}</Text>
    </Box>
  ))}
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 566, left: 60, width: 1160, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', gap: 12 }}>
    <Box style={{ width: 4, height: 40, background: '#1E4FA8' }} />
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.4, width: 1130 }}>Success criteria fixed in advance: scaffold-split R² above 0.5 and screening AUROC above 0.85, and conformal coverage that can be predicted from the applicability domain.</Text>
  </Box>
  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 672, left: 60, width: 1160, flexDirection: 'row' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8B97A8' }}>AIDD8122 Final Project — Trust Before Throughput</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 12, color: '#8B97A8', marginLeft: 'auto' }}>04 / 15</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
